// Farming: bringing a returning player's patches up to date (Corey, 2026-09-05).
//
// Crops grow in real time whether or not anyone is logged in, so the first thing that has to happen
// on login is replaying whatever happened while the player was away. After that a one-minute timer
// keeps things current while they are online, which matters because a patch has to already be in
// the right state by the time they walk up to it - the client draws it straight from the varbit.

[proc,farming_login]
~farming_update_all;
settimer(farming_tick, ^farming_tick_interval);
